{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed the open gap on the retry-growth investigation and upgraded it from unresolved to an asserted, scoped defect, with a fixed experiment submitted to confirm the measurement under the controller. Source answer: the ReadIndex contract (node.go:218-224) states no retry bound, admission is context-blind (read_only.go addRequest appends; stepLeader queues the raw message), ReadOnlySafe is the zero value of ReadOnlyOption and CheckQuorum defaults to false, so a quorum-less leader stays in StateLeader indefinitely and the pending queue is never bounded by step-down; checkQuorum would bound it only if set. A focused probe against the real FSM (repeated by the new experiment) showed a legitimate three-voter leader at term 1 with committed=0/lastIndex=1, CheckQuorum=false and default ReadOnlySafe, where 64 same-context retries produced pending=64 with no collapsing, and pending_after=64 after a higher-term heartbeat deposed it to StateFollower - so the accumulation is neither bounded nor reclaimed by raft.reset. The claim is scoped to accumulation and retention (not answering without quorum remains correct), severity is explicitly unassessed, and the earlier unresolved account is superseded.\"}"}}
